    "threads": [
      {
        "thread_id": "TH1",
        "thread_goal": "Align on current customer journey and main pain points across channels.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M1",
            "speaker_id": 394531,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Hi team, let's kick off the 'Cross-Channel Customer Experience Upgrade' project. To get started on T1, can everyone share their perspective on the current customer journey? What are the most common friction points you see in your area?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "wave",
                "count": 3
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M2",
            "speaker_id": 200631,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "Good start. From a seller's view, the biggest gap is the handover from the contact center. A customer calls with a problem, gets sent to the store, but we have zero context on the issue. They have to explain everything all over again. It's frustrating for them and us.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "point_up",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M3",
            "speaker_id": 45990,
            "reply_to": "M2",
            "text": "I see that every day. Another one is inconsistent information on promotions. A customer sees one price online or hears it from an account manager, but in-store our system shows something different. It makes us look disorganized.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "heavy_plus_sign",
                "count": 3
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M4",
            "speaker_id": 4222,
            "reply_to": "M2",
            "text": "I agree about the handover issue. On our side, we don't have a clear process for what information to capture before sending someone to a store. We log what we can, but there's no standard template.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M5",
            "speaker_id": 24573,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "From the crop production side, we sometimes get customers asking about product origins or details we don't have. We have to tell them to call the main number, which isn't a great experience.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M6",
            "speaker_id": 49060,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "My customers are mostly B2B, so it's a bit different. They just want their orders on time. Sometimes they complain about the delivery process.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M7",
            "speaker_id": 394531,
            "reply_to": "M6",
            "text": "That's a valid point, but for this project, let's focus on the direct customer-facing interactions that the playbook will cover. The handover, inconsistent info, and lack of context seem to be the recurring themes.",
            "mentions": [
              49060
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "ok_hand",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M8",
            "speaker_id": 200631,
            "reply_to": "M7",
            "text": "Exactly. And how we handle complaints. Right now it's ad-hoc. We don't have a consistent way to log feedback. I bet the issues in the A5 log are all over the place.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M9",
            "speaker_id": 394531,
            "reply_to": "M8",
            "text": "Great points everyone. Based on this, I've sketched out a high-level journey map. It's basically: Awareness -> Inquiry (Contact Center/Web) -> Visit (Store/Field Sales) -> Purchase -> Post-Sale Support. The pain points seem to cluster at the Inquiry-to-Visit handover and during Post-Sale Support.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "white_check_mark",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M10",
            "speaker_id": 45990,
            "reply_to": "M9",
            "text": "That map makes sense. It covers the main stages I see.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M11",
            "speaker_id": 394531,
            "reply_to": "M10",
            "text": "Okay, let's formalize this. Proposal for our priority pain points: 1) Inconsistent information across channels (promos, product details), 2) Poor handover of customer context between channels, and 3) No standard process for logging or resolving complaints. Does everyone agree on these three?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D1"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M12",
            "speaker_id": 200631,
            "reply_to": "M11",
            "text": "Yes, those are the big three. They cover 90% of the issues.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 3
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M13",
            "speaker_id": 4222,
            "reply_to": "M11",
            "text": "Agreed.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M14",
