      {
        "thread_id": "TH4",
        "thread_goal": "Plan pilot, training sessions, and feedback collection approach.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M51",
            "speaker_id": 4222,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Hello team, we need to start planning the pilot (T11) and training sessions (T9). I was thinking we could run the pilot for one week. What do you think?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T11",
              "T9"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M52",
            "speaker_id": 394531,
            "reply_to": "M51",
            "text": "Good to get this moving. A one-week pilot sounds right. To make it effective, we need to be specific. Which stores and which sales accounts will participate? We need a mix of high and low traffic locations to get good data. Also, how will we track feedback? We should use the A5 log for this.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "thinking_face",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M53",
            "speaker_id": 200631,
            "reply_to": "M52",
            "text": "I suggest the downtown flagship store for high traffic, and the suburban mall location for a more typical environment. For field sales, we can use two of my accounts that are generally receptive to new processes. This will give us a good test of the A4 visit script.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "bulb",
